.TH "GIT-BUG" "1" "Apr 2019" "Generated from git-bug's source code" ""

.SH NAME
git-bug-pr-head - Record a new head commit of a pull request


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-bug pr head PR_ID [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Record a new head commit of a pull request. Without --commit, the head is the current commit of the source branch.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--commit\fP=""
	Full ID of the commit to record (default: the current commit of the source branch)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for head


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--no-colors\fP[=]
	Do not color the output


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-bug-pr(1)\fP
